# Phase 71 follow-up — greeter background asset policy.
#
# `background.png` IS committed at this directory — a shared boot
# artifact so fresh clones and CI runs all paint the same login
# screen. To change the rendered background you have three real
# options (the greeter prefers PNG first, so simply adding a BMP
# alongside the committed PNG will not take effect on its own):
#
# 1. Replace `background.png` in this directory and commit the new
#    image (the durable shared-asset path).
# 2. Locally remove or rename `background.png` and drop a BMP here.
#    `populate_ext2_files` will stage the BMP and the greeter will
#    decode it via the `.bmp` fallback in `DEFAULT_BACKGROUND_PATHS`.
# 3. Point `background=/your/path` in `/etc/greeter.conf` at any
#    image already on the data disk; the config-driven path wins
#    over both file-name conventions.
#
# Only `background.bmp` is ignored so option (2) above stays a
# zero-touch local override without polluting the repo.
background.bmp
